			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				147,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(license): update project license to LPL\n\nChanged the license field in tauri.conf.json from CC0 to LPL to align with Land's revised licensing strategy. This update ensures proper open source compliance for the Tauri-based distribution while maintaining compatibility with VS Code's extension ecosystem requirements. The LICENSE file reference remains unchanged, indicating full license text continues to be bundled with distributions.\n\nThis licensing adjustment supports Land's goal of creating a sustainable open-core model while preserving the performance-focused migration from Electron. The LPL (Land Public License) likely introduces specific terms regarding commercial use and extension redistribution that better fit the project's long-term maintainership plans compared to the more permissive CC0 license.",
			"SHA": "a5e649a3ff1096f4e97ae1843d56a691630188fe"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-10T14:16:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				147,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(LICENSE): Refine formatting and terminology\n\n- Bolded key terms (e.g. \"Land Public License\" → \"**Land** **Public** **License**\") to improve visual distinction of license-specific terminology\n- Restructured definitions to consistently emphasize LPL-specific components vs External Works, aligning with Art 5's copyleft boundaries\n- Clarified patent grant exclusions regarding External Works to match architectural separation goals in Land's extension model\n- Improved compatibility section formatting for better readability of inbound/outbound license relationships\n- Maintained all substantive legal provisions while enhancing document structure to support Land's open collaboration ecosystem\n\nThese changes strengthen the license's presentation without altering legal intent, supporting clearer third-party contributor understanding as the project grows.",
			"SHA": "9c73f889588db69c6a2ba821cec1d0b753001f1d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-10T14:07:12Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				147,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(license): Correct spelling of 'License' throughout document\n\n- Standardize spelling from 'Licence' to 'License' in all instances within LICENSE file to align with American English conventions\n- Maintain consistent terminology in legal documentation to prevent ambiguity\n- Update preamble, definitions, and cross-references while preserving original legal intent\n- Ensure all section headers and variable references use 'License' spelling\n- No substantive changes to license terms or conditions - purely grammatical correction\n- Improves professionalism and clarity for contributors/licensees reviewing project's legal foundation",
			"SHA": "f00d471af9b8b8fa35c0d8a58c5673d177be1c99"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-10T14:03:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				147,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(LICENSE): improve formatting and structure\n\n- Restructured section 6 with consistent hyphen-based lists and proper indentation for subpoints (6.1-6.4)\n- Fixed nested list formatting in section 11(e) to clarify component identification requirements\n- Added line breaks between license acceptance conditions in section 10(b) for better readability\n\nThese changes enhance document clarity while maintaining legal intent, critical for Land's open-source compliance as a VS Code derivative. Improved formatting reduces ambiguity for contributors interacting with Mountain backend and Cocoon extension host components.",
			"SHA": "8e5fc5ce1e4aedf77981b4822ac0f4c8f55d0430"
		},
