			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				147,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(build): relax CSP for development and production environments\n\n- Set production `csp` to null to use Tauri's default security policies while maintaining VS Code UI compatibility\n- Disabled `dangerousDisableAssetCspModification` to allow Tauri's automatic CSP adjustments for extension resources\n- Added 'unsafe-inline' to dev CSP script-src to support VS Code's webview architecture during development\n\nThese changes balance security requirements with the needs of the Sky frontend's VS Code-derived UI components and future extension loading through Cocoon. The development CSP relaxation enables proper rendering of webviews and script execution patterns used by VS Code's web technologies, while production configuration leverages Tauri's security defaults with explicit exceptions removed.\n\nRefs #123 (security policy implementation)",
			"SHA": "98b2f95c2f31c092a6188f45c28657f40e28f481"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-06T07:41:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				147,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(tauri): Adjust CSP policies to support VS Code extension resources\n\n- Added vscode-remote-resource: and vscode-managed-remote-resource: sources to img-src and font-src directives to allow extension-hosted assets\n- Enabled https: in connect-src and img-src for secure external resource loading\n- Added vscode-webview: to frame-src to support webview communication patterns\n- Set dangerousDisableAssetCspModification to true to permit dynamic CSP updates required by VS Code extension APIs\n- Maintained core security restrictions (trusted-types, unsafe-eval containment) while enabling extension functionality\n\nThis change ensures Cocoon extension host compatibility by aligning CSP rules with VS Code's resource loading patterns while preserving Tauri's security model. Required for proper operation of remote extensions and webview-based UI components.",
			"SHA": "1ec162efd20a8b68d5ec15807b628f362e14a504"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-06T06:32:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				147,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Build): harden webview content security policy\n\n- Added comprehensive CSP rules to Tauri configuration to mitigate XSS risks while maintaining required functionality for Land's editor UI and extension host\n- Allows 'unsafe-eval' and blob: scripts to support VS Code's AMD loader system and extension web workers\n- Enables WebSocket connections via 'wss://tauri.localhost' for Vine IPC layer communication\n- Implements strict trusted-types policy to maintain DOM XSS protections while permitting VS Code UI patterns\n- Maintains 'unsafe-inline' styles required by existing VS Code CSS architecture during migration phase\n- Aligns with Tauri security best practices while preserving compatibility with Cocoon extension host requirements",
			"SHA": "02f7aeea4cf19f2d4c2812006fb09b6b75e398d9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-06T05:51:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠃⠀⠀",
				147,
				66
			],
			"Message": "chore(build): update application branding and updater configuration\n\n- Changed window title from \"Editor\" to \"FIDDEE\" in Tauri configuration to align with product branding\n- Enabled `allowDowngrades` in updater settings to permit installation of older versions during testing phases\n- Updated application icon file (icon.icns) with revised branding assets\n\nThese changes support consistent product identity presentation in the Mountain backend while maintaining development flexibility through the updater configuration. The title update ensures proper window identification in the Sky frontend, while downgrade capability facilitates smoother testing workflows for the Cocoon extension host environment.",
			"SHA": "64565ff763195a3ed2dd0555e68d92c812666216"
