			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				167,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat: Enhance security and UI configuration for browser instance\n\n- Added content protection to prevent unauthorized capture of sensitive data\n- Enabled zoom hotkey support while disabling browser extensions to balance usability with security\n- Implemented borderless window decorations with shadow effect for modern visual presentation\n- Maintained HTTPS enforcement and maximized window state from previous configuration",
			"SHA": "1f3926cf825a46eeaf2112c1712f9d3749b2dc27"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-04T02:09:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				167,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix: Disable default Content Security Policy\n\nThe existing Content Security Policy (CSP) configuration was causing unexpected resource blocking and development friction due to its strict restrictions. This commit removes the CSP by setting it to null to:\n\n1. Resolve issues with legitimate resource loading during application runtime\n2. Eliminate conflicts with required 'unsafe-eval' and 'unsafe-inline' patterns in development environment\n3. Allow temporary permissive access while a more targeted security policy is being developed\n\nThis change prioritizes immediate functionality over security restrictions, with acknowledgment that a proper CSP should be re-implemented post-evaluation of actual resource requirements.",
			"SHA": "fc5edcd19c2938d3196b657cf504c97ff33b3a77"
		},
